notes.content:
Our game has been out for less then a week and we are extremely grateful to your reviews, feedback and support! Since day 1 of release, we immediately started collecting player feedback on issues with the game that they may have found. We started working on all of these in order to improve the most common problems reported. Today we release Patch 1.02 of the game!

[b]Full Changelog:[/b]
- Added a new area you can go to if you decide not to answer The Developer's final question;
- Fixed major bug with doors not opening after player loads a checkpoint - for example the elevator door;
- Slight increase of the zoom-in ability;
- Improved localization;
- Increased the number of checkpoints, if player gets stuck in a level they can reload from a nearest point;
- Fix collision on staircase door where players could get stuck;
- Added a way to get out of the target area in the Introspective Therapy room;
- Added sound feedback in the settings menu to indicate when a setting has gone into effect;
- Small CPU performance optimization;
- Added a hint about the controls in the Annoying Objects Room;
- Added a hint if you can't find the first key code for 10 minutes;
- Cake or Real? game door opens quicker now when you complete the game;

Have fun, dear players!

Thank you for your feedback on the game! We have released a Patch 1.01 based on the first 24 hours of player feedback. We tried to address as many issues as possible.
Thank you for your support and help!

Things that we fixed with this patch

Things that we fixed with this patch

- added more Checkpoint Save Points, so people can load easily if something goes wrong;
- added Invert Mouse and Mouse Sensitivity Options;
- fixed small issues that cause low FPS;
- bug fixed: not being able to continue in Lawn Mower Game when you have the duck;
- bug fixed: some walls not loaded after cake or real room and player can fall off the map;
- spelling mistakes in subtitles corrected;
